From 773fc30d966d326c7902fa2997bcc9797d5ff092 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jon <resands@proton.me>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 13:49:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] iop: native mixer follows PCSX2's SPU2; SPU2 backend hook for
 a reference SPU2

Checked offline against PCSX2's SPU2 core driven by the real libsd (PoP tools/iop/pcsx2_ref):
- envelope and volume sweep: PCSX2 V_ADSR::Calculate / V_VolumeSlide::Update (phase, counter minimum);
  a voice whose sustain reaches 0 stops
- reverb: one side per output sample, position and side from the global sample count (kept across mode
  changes), PCSX2's 39-tap down/up resampling; with effects off it still runs and sounds, writing nothing back
- EVOL is a plain volume (was swept and doubled: reverb 2x too loud)
- a started input is heard from the next 256-sample half of the input ring (hardware latency)

Spu2Backend (ps2x/iop/spu2_backend.h, IopEmulator::setSpu2Backend): every SPU2 register access, DMA and time
step goes to another SPU2 instead of the emulated one. admaWrite takes the IOP cycle.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_012y1nSeB5ALWKBgL9yiuaYc
